);\n-    c.put(\"e\".into(), \"5\".into()); // evicts c\n+    c.put(\"e\".into(), \"5\".into()); // evicts c -> [a, d, e]\n     assert_eq!(c.get(\"c\"), None);\n     assert_eq!(c.evictions(), 2);\n }\n \n","additions":3,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","time":{"start":1789578582834,"end":1789578582840}},"id":"prt_0ab32088200148oWmk4mynkgJr","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","messageID":"msg_0ab31dcce001sKTolj9iXu3ICG"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1789578582917,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab31e66e001KoRcnp6GiZlnfG","messageID":"msg_0ab31dcce001sKTolj9iXu3ICG","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","type":"text","text":"Two tests failed. The `update_moves_to_newest` test is wrong: when cap is 3 and you put a, b, c, then put a (existing, so it just gets marked newest without evicting), the order becomes b, c, a. Then putting d (new) evicts b, and c remains. But my test asserted that `get(\"a\")` returns None, which was a mistake in the test.\nWait, let me re-check.\n- put a -> [a]\n- put b -> [a, b]\n- put c -> [a, b, c]\n- put a (existing) -> marks a newest -> [b, c, a]\n- put d (new, at capacity) -> evicts b -> [c, a, d]\nSo get(\"a\") = Some(\"11\"), get(\"b\") = None, get(\"c\") = Some(\"3\"), get(\"d\") = Some(\"4\")\n\nMy test asserted get(\"a\") == None which is wrong. Let me fix the test.\n\nThe second failing test `large_scale_churn`: cap=1_000_000, n=5_000_000. The test checks `get(\"key-4000000\")` (i.e., n - 1_000_000). After putting keys key-0 to key-4999999, the first 4_000_000 are evicted, and key-4000000 to key-4999999 remain. So key-4000000 should be in the cache! That's exactly n - 1_000_000 = 4_000_000.\n\nWait, the test asserted `assert_eq!(c.get(&format!(\"key-{}\", n - 1_000_000)), None)` but the key-4000000 was NOT evicted because it's exactly at the boundary. The remaining keys are key-4000000 to key-4999999. So key-4000000 should be in the cache, not None. The test assertion was wrong - it should be Some(\"value-4000000\").\n\nWait, the error says \"left: Some(\"value-4000000\"), right: None\" - left is c.get result = Some(\"value-4000000\") and right is None. So the cache correctly returned Some(\"value-4000000\") but the test expected None. The test expectation was wrong.\n\nLet me fix both tests.\n\n","time":{"start":1789578569326,"end":1789578582906}}}
