{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789578616462,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab329e8b001BGZoQgENeHNRIu","messageID":"msg_0ab329444001qZ1vyGlZW5meXe","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1789578624130,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab329e8c001GYWfQv29un9SqZ","messageID":"msg_0ab329444001qZ1vyGlZW5meXe","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","type":"text","text":"The test expects `get(\"a\")` to return `Some(\"11\")`, but my implementation returned `None` — the reason being that in `mark_newest`, `rotate_left(pos)` moves element `pos` to the front, so the element ends up placed at the front rather than at the tail. Since the `VecDeque` front represents the oldest element, moving `a` to the front marks it as the oldest, not the newest. What I actually need is to move it to the back. Fix: `rotate_left` is wrong. Instead I should use `rotate_left(len - pos - 1)`, or more simply, remove it and re-push.\n\n","time":{"start":1789578616460,"end":1789578624129}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789578624144,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_080ac3d033bd43e08a21b86f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","newString":"    fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n        if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n        }\n    }","oldString":"    fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n        if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n            self.recency.rotate_left(pos);\n        }\n    }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n+++ /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n@@ -51,9 +51,9 @@\n     }\n \n     fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n         if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n-            self.recency.rotate_left(pos);\n+            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n+++ /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n@@ -51,9 +51,9 @@\n     }\n \n     fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n         if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n-            self.recency.rotate_left(pos);\n+            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs"