{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789578647432,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_7035a63359d4432ab74feefd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","newString":"    fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n        if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n            let item = self.recency.remove(pos).unwrap();\n            self.recency.push_back(item);\n        }\n    }","oldString":"    fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n        if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n        }\n    }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n+++ /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n@@ -51,9 +51,10 @@\n     }\n \n     fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n         if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n-            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n+            let item = self.recency.remove(pos).unwrap();\n+            self.recency.push_back(item);\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n+++ /tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs\n@@ -51,9 +51,10 @@\n     }\n \n     fn mark_newest(&mut self, key: &str) {\n         if let Some(pos) = self.recency.iter().position(|k| k == key) {\n-            self.recency.rotate_left(self.recency.len() - pos - 1);\n+            let item = self.recency.remove(pos).unwrap();\n+            self.recency.push_back(item);\n         }\n     }\n }\n \n","additions":2,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-ON-1/work/src/lib.rs","time":{"start":1789578647424,"end":1789578647430}},"id":"prt_0ab3317780011ho2q9PRJqGErq","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","messageID":"msg_0ab32e1b6001Z3hzjrTQsUdzIH"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1789578647484,"sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab32eb49001562Rt4PCUxz8Ex","messageID":"msg_0ab32e1b6001Z3hzjrTQsUdzIH","sessionID":"ses_f54d012c1ffeVAia3LAf67snK5","type":"text","text":"The `rotate_left` approach seems to still have issues. Let me think through it more carefully.\n\nRecency order: front = oldest, back = newest. Initial state after a, b, c: [a, b, c].\n\n`put a` (existing): `mark_newest(\"a\")`. `pos = 0`. `len - pos - 1 = 3 - 0 - 1 = 2`. `rotate_left(2)`: [a, b, c] → [c, a, b]. This puts `a` in the middle! Not correct.\n\n`rotate_left(n)` on VecDeque shifts left: the element at index n moves to the front. So `rotate_left(2)` means the element at index 2 (c) moves to front: [c, a, b]. That's not what I wanted. I wanted `a` to go to the end.\n\nTo move element at position `pos` to the end, I need to rotate left by `len - pos`. Let me verify: `len - pos = 3 - 0 = 3`. `rotate_left(3)` on [a,b,c] is the same as no rotation (full cycle) → [a, b, c]. That's wrong too, wait.\n\nHmm, `rotate_left` with `n` rotates left by `n` positions. If `n == len` that's a full rotation = identity. So `len - pos` when pos=0 gives 3 = full rotation, which is identity, and a stays at front. Not correct.\n\nWait let me reconsider. I want to move the element at index `pos` to the end. Using `rotate_left`:\n- `rotate_left(k)` makes element at index `k` become the new front.\n- To make element at index `pos` the new back: after `rotate_left(pos)`, the element at `pos` is at the front, and the original elements `[0..pos)` become the last `pos` elements. So the rotation puts the element at `pos` at front, not back.\n\nActually, to move element at `pos` to the end, I can use `rotate_left(len - pos)` which puts the element at index `len - pos` to the front... that doesn't work either.\n\nThe simplest correct approach: remove the element at `pos` and re-push to the back.\n```\nlet item = self.recency.remove(pos).unwrap();\nself.recency.push_back(item);\n```\n\nThis is O(n) worst case for VecDeque (middle removal is O(n)), but it's correct. Let me just use that instead.\n\n","time":{"start":1789578636105,"end":1789578647472}}}
